# =============================================================================
# db/.dockerignore
#
# db/Dockerfile copies NOTHING: it derives from the official postgres image and
# removes one unreachable binary. Excluding the whole context keeps the build
# reproducible and keeps db/init/01-create-service-roles.sh - which is mounted at
# RUN time by docker-compose.yml, never baked into a layer - out of the image.
#
# `*` with no re-admission is therefore the complete and correct policy. The root
# .gitignore still governs what is committed here; this file governs only what
# Docker may read.
# =============================================================================
*
